          "Can read taught n patterns accurately and increasingly smoothly while retaining comprehension, with remaining needs identified.",
          "Can correct diagnosed /n/ decoding, spelling, fluency or comprehension needs and demonstrate improvement before advancing.",
          "Can hear short /i/, distinguish it from /a/, and connect it to i.",
          "Can decode controlled CVC words with short /i/ and distinguish /i/ from /a/ during reading.",
          "Can segment and spell taught CVC words containing short /i/ and self-check through read-back.",
          "Can recognize -it and -in patterns while decoding each complete short /i/ word accurately.",
          "Can read controlled short /i/ sentences and answer literal who, what and where questions using text evidence.",
          "Can read a controlled short /i/ passage, sequence key events and support details with text evidence.",
          "Can demonstrate short /i/ sound, decoding, spelling and comprehension readiness and identify any component requiring remediation.",
          "Can remediate a diagnosed short /i/ weakness and demonstrate readiness through fresh reassessment evidence.",
          "Can hear short /o/ in taught CVC examples and connect the sound to grapheme o.",
          "Can decode taught short /o/ CVC words by saying each grapheme sound, blending, and self-correcting vowel errors.",
          "Can segment and spell taught short /o/ CVC words and self-check through read-back.",
          "Can recognize -ot, -op and -og patterns while decoding each complete short /o/ word accurately.",
          "Can read controlled short /o/ sentences and answer literal questions using text evidence.",
          "Can read a controlled short /o/ passage, sequence key events and support details with text evidence.",
          "Can demonstrate short /o/ sound, decoding, spelling and comprehension readiness and identify any component requiring remediation.",
          "Can remediate a diagnosed short /o/ weakness and demonstrate readiness through fresh reassessment evidence.",
          "Can hear and identify short /e/ and connect the phoneme to grapheme e in controlled CVC words.",
